# AICAD on a developer machine (Ollama).
#
# Production is vLLM on ARUCAD hardware — see ../README.md. This file is the
# local-development equivalent: the same OpenAI-compatible contract, served by
# Ollama, so `AI_PROVIDER=local` works on a laptop with no code change.
#
# Build it (from the repository root):
#
#   ollama create aicad-qwen3:8b -f deploy/ai/ollama/aicad-qwen3-8b.Modelfile
#
# then point the backend at it:
#
#   LOCAL_AI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
#   LOCAL_AI_MODEL=aicad-qwen3:8b

FROM qwen3:8b

# THE REASON THIS FILE EXISTS.
#
# Ollama defaults to a 4096-token context and silently truncates anything
# longer — from the FRONT. AICAD's system prompt measures 6,234 tokens on its
# own (AskPromptBuilder: rules, metadata, personal block, retrieved sources),
# so on the default context two thirds of it was discarded before the model
# ever saw it, and what was discarded was the beginning: the language rule,
# the "never invent a number" rule, the source-priority order, the markdown
# ban and the prompt-injection fence that marks retrieved web text as data
# rather than instructions. The model still answered — plausibly, in markdown,
# with none of its guardrails — which is exactly why this was worth measuring
# rather than assuming.
#
# 12288 holds the prompt plus ai.history_turns of conversation and the reply.
# On an 8 GB card that spills ~13% of the layers to CPU (≈21 tok/s instead of
# ≈33). That is the right trade: a fast answer produced with the rules missing
# is worse than a slower answer produced with them present. On a 12 GB+ card
# raise this to 16384; do not lower it below the prompt size.
PARAMETER num_ctx 12288

# THE OTHER HALF OF THE SPEED.
#
# Ollama sizes the GPU offload itself and is conservative about it. On this
# 8 GB card it placed 87% of the model on the GPU and left the rest on the
# CPU — with 1.1 GB of VRAM still unused. Those few CPU layers cost more than
# they save: every generated token waits on them.
#
# Measured, same prompt, same card, f16 KV cache:
#
#   default offload (87% GPU)   20.3 tok/s   ~20 s for a 300-token answer
#   num_gpu 99   (100% GPU)     32.3 tok/s   ~14 s        "
#
# 99 means "every layer"; llama.cpp clamps it to the number the model has.
# If a future model does not fit, Ollama fails to load rather than silently
# spilling — which is the better failure, because the spill is invisible and
# this is exactly what it costs.
#
# NOT to be confused with quantising the KV cache, which was also measured
# here and is a trap on this workload: OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0 did reach
# 100% GPU and 30 tok/s, but prompt processing went from 2.1 s to 39 s
# because our prompt is ~6,200 tokens and quantised KV has to be dequantised
# during prefill. End to end that was four times SLOWER. Leave the KV cache
# at f16.
PARAMETER num_gpu 99

# Sampling. Kept identical to aicad-qwen3:4b so switching LOCAL_AI_MODEL
# between them changes the model and nothing else. temperature is normally
# supplied per-request by the backend (LOCAL_AI_TEMPERATURE); the rest are
# not, so they are pinned here.
PARAMETER temperature 0.1
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.05
